-- title:
--   Special fibres of the two Igusa chart algebras
-- statement:
--   Fix $N \ge 1$ and a prime $\ell$ with $\ell \nmid N$, and let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ lying over $\ell$ in the sense that $\ell$ belongs to the nonunits of $A$; assume moreover that the residue field $k = \mathrm{ResidueField}\,A$ has characteristic $\ell$ and is algebraically closed. Let $\rho$ be a ring homomorphism from $\mathbb Z_{(\ell)} =$ [`GaloisRep.ratLocalizedAt ℓ`](def/GaloisRep_Flat.html#L8), the subring of rationals whose denominator is coprime to $\ell$, into $A$, and assume that $\rho$ followed by the inclusion $A \hookrightarrow \overline{\mathbb Q}$ is the canonical structure map, so that $\rho$ is the restriction of that embedding. Give $k$ the $\mathbb Z_{(\ell)}$-algebra structure coming from $\rho$ followed by the residue map. Write $F =$ `modularFunctionFieldFull N` $\subset \mathbb Q((q))$, $j =$ `jFull N` its $j$-expansion element, and let `chartAlgFin N ℓ`, `chartAlgInf N ℓ` be the subalgebras of $F$ consisting of the elements integral over $\mathbb Z_{(\ell)}[j]$, respectively over $\mathbb Z_{(\ell)}[j^{-1}]$. On the characteristic-$\ell$ side let $\tilde j =$ `jqModC k`, the Laurent series $q^{-1}\cdot(E_4^3\,\eta^{-24})$ with coefficients reduced into $k$, viewed as an element of the intermediate field $F_N(k) =$ `modularFunctionFieldFullC k N`, the $k$-subextension of $k((q))$ generated by the divisor expansions, and let `CurveModel.chartRing k S` denote the subalgebra of elements of that field integral over $k[S]$. The assertion is twofold: first, there is a $k$-algebra isomorphism $$k \otimes_{\mathbb Z_{(\ell)}} \mathrm{chartAlgFin}\,N\,\ell \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \mathrm{chartRing}\,k\,\{\tilde j\}$$ carrying $1 \otimes j$ to $\tilde j$; second, there is a $k$-algebra isomorphism $$k \otimes_{\mathbb Z_{(\ell)}} \mathrm{chartAlgInf}\,N\,\ell \;\xrightarrow{\ \sim\ }\; \mathrm{chartRing}\,k\,\{\tilde j^{-1}\}$$ carrying $1 \otimes j^{-1}$ to $\tilde j^{-1}$, both identifications of elements being read in $F_N(k)$.
--
--   This is the chart-by-chart identification of the special fibre of the Igusa scheme over $\mathbb Z_{(\ell)}$ with Igusa's curve in characteristic $\ell$: the reduction of the integral closure of $\mathbb Z_{(\ell)}[j]$ (respectively $\mathbb Z_{(\ell)}[j^{-1}]$) in the modular function field is the integral closure of $k[\tilde j]$ (respectively $k[\tilde j^{-1}]$) in the characteristic-$\ell$ modular function field, the arithmetic content of good reduction of the modular curve at primes not dividing the level. It is used by the level-ring constructions [`ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_algEquiv_residueField_tensor_quotient_span_natCast_chartRing`](thm.html#ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_algEquiv_residueField_tensor_quotient_span_natCast_chartRing) and [`ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_ringHom_laurentSeries_ker_eq_span_natCast`](thm.html#ModularCurve.HpoolLevelRing.exists_ringHom_laurentSeries_ker_eq_span_natCast), and by the construction of retraction pairs for the finite chart.
